+CONTEXT.md:15:**Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository**:
+CONTEXT.md:16:A Product Repository that also acts as a Workspace Repository for running Personal Symphony against its own work.
+CONTEXT.md:20:The first-time setup of Personal Symphony runtime files inside a Workspace Repository.
+CONTEXT.md:24:The `.symphony/` directory that contains Personal Symphony configuration and runtime-owned files for a Workspace Repository.
+CONTEXT.md:31:**Agent Worktree**:
+CONTEXT.md:35:**Loop-Start Branch**:
+CONTEXT.md:36:The Workspace Repository branch that is checked out when orchestration starts.
+CONTEXT.md:39:**Task Branch**:
+CONTEXT.md:40:A Git branch created from the Loop-Start Branch for one dispatched task.
+CONTEXT.md:43:**Task Branch Prefix**:
+CONTEXT.md:44:The configured Git branch namespace used for Task Branch names.
+CONTEXT.md:51:**Human Attention Status**:
+CONTEXT.md:56:The Human Attention Status used when agent work completed but its Task Branch could not be auto-merged.
+CONTEXT.md:59:**Manual Task Merge**:
+CONTEXT.md:60:A one-shot operator CLI action that integrates explicitly selected completed Agent Worktrees or Task Branches into the current Loop-Start Branch.
+CONTEXT.md:68:The ignored `.symphony/.env` file that stores local secret values for a Workspace Repository.
+CONTEXT.md:71:**Runtime Contract**:
+CONTEXT.md:72:The repository-owned files inside the Runtime Home that define Personal Symphony behavior for a Workspace Repository.
+CONTEXT.md:75:**Runtime Settings**:
+CONTEXT.md:76:The `settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract that defines tracker, project, orchestration, agent, server, and path configuration.
+CONTEXT.md:80:The Runtime Settings section that defines Task Branch and Protected Trunk Branch behavior.
+CONTEXT.md:83:**Allowed Loop-Start Branch Policy**:
+CONTEXT.md:84:A Runtime Settings rule that identifies which Loop-Start Branches may dispatch automated orchestration.
+CONTEXT.md:87:**Protected Path Policy**:
+CONTEXT.md:88:A repository-owned rule that identifies Workspace Repository paths agent work must not modify without explicit authorization.
+CONTEXT.md:96:The `prompt.md` portion of the Runtime Contract that defines the task instructions rendered for each dispatched issue.
+CONTEXT.md:103:**Stage Commit**:
+CONTEXT.md:107:**Stage Commit Classification**:
+CONTEXT.md:108:Repository-owned metadata used to choose the commit type or tag for a Stage Commit.
+CONTEXT.md:112:An optional push of a Stage Commit to the currently checked-out Task Branch after the Stage Commit is created.
+CONTEXT.md:116:A Runtime Settings rule that limits how many agents may run for a specific Stage Agent.
+CONTEXT.md:143:**Batch Pull Request**:
+CONTEXT.md:144:A single pull request opened from the Loop-Start Branch after Symphony reaches Orchestration Idle.
+CONTEXT.md:148:An optional non-force push of the Loop-Start Branch before opening a Batch Pull Request.
+CONTEXT.md:152:The configured target branch for a Batch Pull Request.
+CONTEXT.md:156:The Runtime Settings section that controls automatic Batch Pull Request creation.
+CONTEXT.md:160:The configured title or body pattern used when opening a Batch Pull Request.
+CONTEXT.md:168:A Loop-Start Branch checkout with no uncommitted Workspace Repository changes.
+CONTEXT.md:171:**Startup Reconciliation**:
+CONTEXT.md:172:The startup-time recovery pass that checks completed-stage Agent Worktrees for Task Branch commits not present on the Loop-Start Branch.
+CONTEXT.md:175:**Task Branch Integration**:
+CONTEXT.md:176:The serialized act of bringing completed Task Branch commits into the Loop-Start Branch, directly by fast-forward when possible or by first updating the Task Branch from the current Loop-Start Branch.
