+CONTEXT.md:239:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may commit a real **Runtime Contract** for its own Personal Symphony runs.
+CONTEXT.md:240:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use a dedicated GitHub Project as its dispatch board.
+CONTEXT.md:241:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may enable **Stage Goal Handoff** on every configured **Stage Agent**.
+CONTEXT.md:242:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may use its planner stage as a PRD review gate for already-refined issues.
+CONTEXT.md:243:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use **Stage Commit** to create local engineer-stage commits before review.
+CONTEXT.md:244:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should keep **Stage Push** disabled unless remote branch publication is deliberately enabled.
+CONTEXT.md:245:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use reviewer-stage comments and a **Human Attention Status** for review findings that require operator triage.
+CONTEXT.md:246:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should have the reviewer stage run focused verification when practical before moving work to `Done`.
+CONTEXT.md:247:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may increase concurrency when its **Loop-Start Branch** is not a **Protected Trunk Branch** because **Task Branch Integration** can integrate unrelated concurrently completed **Task Branches**.
+CONTEXT.md:248:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use a dedicated non-trunk **Loop-Start Branch** so completed **Task Branches** do not auto-merge into the Product Repository trunk.
+CONTEXT.md:249:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may open a **Batch Pull Request** from its dedicated **Loop-Start Branch** to its **Protected Trunk Branch** after **Orchestration Idle**.
+CONTEXT.md:250:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should remove merged **Agent Worktrees** and delete merged **Task Branches** to avoid local branch buildup.
+CONTEXT.md:251:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should prevent accidental dogfood dispatch from the Product Repository trunk.
+CONTEXT.md:252:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should define a **Protected Path Policy** for release and package files once that policy exists.
+CONTEXT.md:253:- An **Idempotent Bootstrap** must preserve existing Runtime Contract and Local Environment files.
+CONTEXT.md:254:- A **Workspace Repository** contains at most one **Runtime Home**.
+CONTEXT.md:255:- Personal Symphony commands must be run from the root of a **Workspace Repository**.
+CONTEXT.md:256:- Personal Symphony exits before Bootstrap when the current directory is not the root of a **Workspace Repository**.
+CONTEXT.md:257:- A **Runtime Home** contains the **Runtime Contract**, user-editable settings, and internal state.
+CONTEXT.md:258:- The **Runtime Contract** contains **Runtime Settings**.
+CONTEXT.md:259:- The **Runtime Contract** contains an **Agent Prompt**.
+CONTEXT.md:263:- An **Agent Worktree** is an **Agent Workspace**.
+CONTEXT.md:264:- The **Runtime Settings** contain a **Git Policy**.
+CONTEXT.md:265:- A **Git Policy** may contain an **Allowed Loop-Start Branch Policy**.
+CONTEXT.md:266:- A **Workspace Repository** may define a **Protected Path Policy**.
+CONTEXT.md:267:- The first **Protected Path Policy** lives in **Runtime Settings**, not in a standalone `.symphonyignore` file.
+CONTEXT.md:268:- **Protected Path Policy** patterns are repository-root-relative and may match files, directories, globs, generated-file paths that would otherwise be committed or integrated, and nested paths.
+CONTEXT.md:269:- The first **Protected Path Policy** does not support negation patterns.
+CONTEXT.md:270:- **Protected Path Policy** checks added, modified, deleted, and renamed paths.
+CONTEXT.md:275:- Each **Agent Worktree** belongs to one dispatched task.
+CONTEXT.md:276:- Agent Worktrees live under the Runtime Home workspaces directory.
+CONTEXT.md:277:- Each **Agent Worktree** checks out one **Task Branch**.
+CONTEXT.md:278:- Each **Task Branch** starts from the **Loop-Start Branch**.
+CONTEXT.md:279:- Each **Task Branch** name starts with the **Task Branch Prefix** and includes the task's stable issue number.
+CONTEXT.md:280:- If a task enters work without an existing **Task Branch**, the **Task Branch** starts from the current **Loop-Start Branch**.
+CONTEXT.md:281:- If a task already has a **Task Branch**, Symphony reuses it.
+CONTEXT.md:282:- A dispatched task has an **Agent Worktree** when it enters the in-progress project state.
+CONTEXT.md:283:- If Symphony starts while a task is already in the in-progress project state, Symphony creates or reuses that task's **Agent Worktree** before starting agent work.
+CONTEXT.md:284:- Symphony requires a **Clean Loop-Start Worktree** before creating an **Agent Worktree**.
+CONTEXT.md:285:- Symphony may auto-merge a completed **Task Branch** into the **Loop-Start Branch** only when the **Loop-Start Branch** is not a **Protected Trunk Branch**.
+CONTEXT.md:286:- Auto-merge of a **Task Branch** into the **Loop-Start Branch** keeps the final **Loop-Start Branch** update fast-forward only.
+CONTEXT.md:287:- If the **Loop-Start Branch** cannot fast-forward directly to a completed **Task Branch**, Symphony may update the **Task Branch** by merging the current **Loop-Start Branch** into it from the **Agent Worktree**, then fast-forward the **Loop-Start Branch** to the updated **Task Branch**.
+CONTEXT.md:289:- Auto-merge, **Startup Reconciliation**, and **Manual Task Merge** are **Task Branch Integration** paths.
+CONTEXT.md:290:- An **Allowed Loop-Start Branch Policy** prevents dispatch from any Loop-Start Branch outside the configured literal branch set.
+CONTEXT.md:291:- An omitted or empty **Allowed Loop-Start Branch Policy** allows any Loop-Start Branch.
+CONTEXT.md:292:- A disallowed **Loop-Start Branch** is a **Readiness Gap** that keeps the **Terminal Console** and **Web Dashboard** available for inspection while blocking dispatch, **Startup Reconciliation**, and **Batch Pull Request** creation.
+CONTEXT.md:293:- **Manual Task Merge** integrates selected completed task work with `--merge` without running normal orchestration.
+CONTEXT.md:294:- **Manual Task Merge** accepts issue identifiers such as `20` and `#20`; it does not accept raw **Task Branch** names.
+CONTEXT.md:295:- **Manual Task Merge** preflights every selected task before merging anything, requires clean Loop-Start and Agent Worktrees, and uses fast-forward-only semantics.
+CONTEXT.md:296:- **Manual Task Merge** may target a **Protected Trunk Branch** because explicit selected issue identifiers are the operator action.
+CONTEXT.md:297:- **Manual Task Merge** does not push branches, run Startup Reconciliation, dispatch agents, or open a Batch Pull Request.
+CONTEXT.md:298:- **Startup Reconciliation** runs once per process startup before normal dispatch or agent launch.
+CONTEXT.md:299:- **Startup Reconciliation** evaluates completed-stage **Agent Worktrees** in deterministic issue order.
+CONTEXT.md:300:- **Startup Reconciliation** uses the same safe **Task Branch Integration** path as normal completion.
+CONTEXT.md:301:- **Startup Reconciliation** does not create a **Stage Commit**, reconcile retained **Task Branches** without **Agent Worktrees**, or change tracker status after successful or already-contained reconciliation.
+CONTEXT.md:302:- **Startup Reconciliation** moves unsafe, contradictory, conflicted, or Protected Trunk Branch candidates to the **Merge Attention Status** and records Runtime State diagnostics.
+CONTEXT.md:303:- **Runtime State** records **Task Branch Integration** diagnostics for direct fast-forwards, update-then-fast-forward integrations, already-contained branches, and integration attention.
+CONTEXT.md:304:- A **Merge Attention Status** is a **Human Attention Status**.
+CONTEXT.md:306:- A **Human Attention Status** is paused and not dispatchable.
+CONTEXT.md:307:- The default **Task Cleanup Policy** removes an **Agent Worktree** after its **Task Branch** is merged.
+CONTEXT.md:308:- The default **Task Cleanup Policy** keeps a merged **Task Branch**.
+CONTEXT.md:309:- A **Stage Commit** may be created when a configured stage completes with code changes.
+CONTEXT.md:310:- A **Stage Commit** may use a **Stage Commit Classification** when rendering its commit message.
+CONTEXT.md:311:- A **Stage Push** happens only after a **Stage Commit** is successfully created.
+CONTEXT.md:313:- Runtime Settings enable a **Stage Push** with `commit.push` on a configured stage.
+CONTEXT.md:315:- Bootstrapped Runtime Settings include `commit.push` as `false` in each example stage commit policy.
+CONTEXT.md:316:- A **Stage Push** sends the **Stage Commit** to the currently checked-out **Task Branch**.
+CONTEXT.md:317:- Symphony checks the **Protected Path Policy** before creating a **Stage Commit**.
+CONTEXT.md:318:- Unauthorized protected path changes move the task to the **Human Attention Status** and prevent **Stage Commit** creation.
+CONTEXT.md:319:- Because **Stage Push** follows **Stage Commit**, unauthorized protected path changes also prevent **Stage Push**.
+CONTEXT.md:320:- **Startup Reconciliation**, **Task Branch Integration**, and **Manual Task Merge** must refuse unauthorized protected path changes before integrating committed **Task Branch** work.
+CONTEXT.md:321:- **Batch Pull Request** creation remains blocked while protected-path attention is unresolved.
+CONTEXT.md:322:- A **Stage Push** pushes the current **Task Branch** tip, including earlier unpushed commits on that branch.
+CONTEXT.md:324:- A **Stage Push** uses the current **Task Branch** upstream when one exists.
+CONTEXT.md:325:- A **Stage Push** creates an upstream on `origin` when the current **Task Branch** has no upstream.
+CONTEXT.md:327:- **Task Branch Integration** must not force-push a **Task Branch** after **Stage Push**.
+CONTEXT.md:328:- Symphony does not push the **Loop-Start Branch** after auto-merge.
+CONTEXT.md:333:- Runtime Settings configure **Stage Goal Handoff** with `goal.enabled` on a stage.
+CONTEXT.md:335:- Bootstrapped Runtime Settings include `goal.enabled` as `false` in each example stage.
+CONTEXT.md:356:- **Stage Goal Handoff** does not change retry, completion, status transition, commit, push, auto-merge, or Batch Pull Request behavior.
+CONTEXT.md:360:- An **Ordered Queue** is named with issue identifiers from the Workspace Repository issue tracker.
+CONTEXT.md:369:- An **Ordered Queue Entry** is invalid when it is malformed, missing from the Workspace Repository issue tracker, absent from the configured GitHub Project, terminal, or not dispatchable.
+CONTEXT.md:382:- Ordered Queue completion may trigger existing **Batch Pull Request** behavior for completed queued work.
+CONTEXT.md:386:- A **Batch Pull Request** represents the combined task work already integrated into the **Loop-Start Branch**.
+CONTEXT.md:387:- Symphony may open a **Batch Pull Request** after reaching **Orchestration Idle**.
+CONTEXT.md:388:- Symphony must not open a **Batch Pull Request** while any issue remains in a **Merge Attention Status**.
+CONTEXT.md:389:- Symphony must not open a **Batch Pull Request** while any issue has unresolved orchestration attention.
+CONTEXT.md:390:- A **Batch Pull Request** uses the **Loop-Start Branch** as its head branch.
+CONTEXT.md:391:- A **Batch Pull Request** uses the configured **Pull Request Base Branch** as its base branch.
+CONTEXT.md:392:- Symphony may retry opening a **Batch Pull Request** after a failed attempt when **Orchestration Idle** is reached again.
+CONTEXT.md:393:- Symphony must not create a duplicate **Batch Pull Request** for the same head and base branches.
+CONTEXT.md:394:- A **Pull Request Base Branch** must be configured explicitly in Runtime Settings.
+CONTEXT.md:395:- The **Runtime Settings** may contain a **Pull Request Policy**.
+CONTEXT.md:396:- The **Pull Request Policy** controls whether Symphony opens a **Batch Pull Request** after **Orchestration Idle**.
+CONTEXT.md:397:- The default **Pull Request Policy** disables automatic **Batch Pull Request** creation.
+CONTEXT.md:398:- A **Pull Request Base Branch** is required when the **Pull Request Policy** enables automatic **Batch Pull Request** creation.
+CONTEXT.md:399:- The **Pull Request Policy** may define **Pull Request Templates** for the **Batch Pull Request** title and body.
+CONTEXT.md:401:- A **Batch Branch Push** happens before opening a **Batch Pull Request**.
+CONTEXT.md:402:- A **Batch Branch Push** pushes the **Loop-Start Branch** to its remote head branch.
+CONTEXT.md:403:- A failed **Batch Branch Push** prevents the **Batch Pull Request** from being opened.
+CONTEXT.md:405:- Runtime State records Batch Pull Request handoff attempts, completions, and retryable failures.
+CONTEXT.md:406:- The **Runtime Contract** is version-controlled with the Workspace Repository.
+CONTEXT.md:427:- **Audio Notification Configuration** does not change **Runtime Settings**.
